  "transcript": [
    {
      "turn": 0,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "Alright, doctor. My stomach's been playing up."
    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Can you tell me more about how your stomach feels? For example, is it painful, bloated, or does it feel like it's twisting?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "It's a burning pain in the upper middle of my tummy, about 5 out of 10. It gets worse an hour after meals and sometimes at night. I feel sick after eating and bloated, but I haven't thrown up.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": [
        "f03",
        "f04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": 2,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Does the pain get better when you take antacids or drink milk?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 2,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "The antacids help a little, but not much. Milk makes it feel worse, like it's burning even more.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": [
        "f08"
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": 3,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you noticed any changes in your bowel movements, like diarrhea, constipation, or black, tarry stools?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 3,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I passed black, sticky, smelly stools twice this week. I haven't had diarrhea or constipation, though I've been feeling like I need to go more often.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": [
        "f05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": 4,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you been taking any medications, supplements, or herbal remedies recently?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 4,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I've been taking ibuprofen 400 mg three times a day for my knee, and I chew antacid tablets a few times a day. I don't take any supplements or herbal remedies.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": [
        "f08"
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": 5,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any recent injuries, falls, or changes in your activity level that might have affected your stomach or digestion?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 5,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I haven't had any falls or injuries. My activity level's been pretty normal, though I've been feeling run down lately.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "turn": 6,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you experienced any weight loss, changes in appetite, or feelings of weakness recently?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 6,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I've lost about 5 pounds in the last month without trying. I don't have much of an appetite, and I feel weak, especially in the afternoons.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "turn": 7,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you noticed any other symptoms, such as dizziness, fatigue, or a feeling of fullness even after eating small amounts?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 7,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I feel dizzy when I stand up fast, and I'm really tired all the time. I also feel full even after eating just a little, like my stomach's swollen.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": [
        "f04",
        "f06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": 8,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any recent changes in your diet, such as eating more spicy, fatty, or acidic foods?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 8,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I've been eating more spicy takeaways and fatty foods because I'm working late a lot. I think it's contributing to my stomach issues.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": [
        "f12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": 9,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any symptoms like nausea, vomiting, or a feeling of something stuck in your throat?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 9,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I feel nauseous after eating, but I haven't vomited. Sometimes I get a weird feeling like something's stuck in my throat, especially when I lie down.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": [
        "f04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": 10,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you noticed any symptoms like chest pain, shortness of breath, or a racing heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 10,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I've had a tight, burning feeling in my chest, especially after eating. I don't think it's heart-related, but it worries me a bit. I haven't had shortness of breath or a racing heart.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "turn": 11,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any symptoms like abdominal swelling, visible veins, or a feeling of pressure in your abdomen?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 11,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "My belly feels swollen, like there's air inside. I don't see any veins, but there's a pressure-like feeling when I press on it.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "turn": 12,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any symptoms like fever, chills, or night sweats?"
    },
    {
      "turn": 12,
      "role": "patient",
      "text": "I haven't had a fever, but I've been sweating a lot at night, especially after my stomach pains. I don't think I've had chills.",
      "gate_selected_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "turn": 13,
      "role": "interviewer",
      "text": "Have you had any symptoms like jaundice (yellowing of the skin or eyes), dark urine, or light-colored stools?  \n\n[HISTORY COMPLETE]"
    }
  ],
